          "distinct": true,
          "id": "451bb4ff5646b3e4c5cb4b77930abf9af574aafc",
          "message": "(feat): new `value_gradient` API for ND Interpolants  (#73)\n\n* feat: Add value_gradient/value_gradient! for locate-once value+gradient computation\n\nAdd value_gradient(itp, query) and value_gradient!(G, itp, query) that compute\nthe interpolant value and gradient in a single call, performing interval search\nonly once. Achieves 20-45% speedup over separate itp(q) + gradient(itp, q) calls.\n\n- @generated implementations with locate-once pattern for all ND interpolants\n- Tuple and Vector query APIs, zero-allocation in-place variant\n- ChainRulesCore rrules for Zygote/Enzyme AD compatibility\n- CubicInterpolantND-specific rrule with ∂/∂data via cubic_adjoint\n\n* refactor: Remove value_gradient!, fix rrule promote_type, add tests\n\n- Remove value_gradient! (non-standard API; value_gradient already\n  zero-alloc via NTuple return; Optim.jl users can use G .= grad)\n- Fix CubicND rrule T_out to include cotangent types in promote_type,\n  preventing silent imaginary-part loss with complex cotangents\n- Add value_gradient docstring with Optim.jl fg! usage pattern\n- Add tests: @inferred type stability, vector-grid consistency,\n  PeriodicBC (exclusive), Zygote non-Cubic rrule path (Linear/Quadratic)\n\n* fix: Guard rrule promote_type against ZeroTangent, add allocation test\n\n- Replace `eltype(Δgrad)` with `map(typeof, Δgrad)...` to prevent\n  abstract type leakage on heterogeneous tangent tuples\n- Guard with `Δgrad isa AbstractZero` check for when only the value\n  part is differentiated (Δgrad arrives as ZeroTangent)\n- Add zero-allocation regression test for value_gradient tuple query\n\n* docs: Add value_gradient to API reference, ND derivatives, and optimization guide\n\n- Add value_gradient to @docs block in api/types.md\n- Add value_gradient section in nd/derivatives.md between gradient and hessian\n- Add locate-once fg! pattern subsection in optimization guide\n- Add value_gradient cross-references in gradient/gradient! docstrings\n\n* fix: value_gradient returns fill_value instead of zero for FillExtrap OOB\n\nFillExtrap(NaN) or FillExtrap(-999) would incorrectly return 0 for the\nvalue part. Now uses _first_fill_value to extract the configured fill\nvalue. Test strengthened with non-zero fill values.",
          "timestamp": "2026-03-10T14:09:19-07:00",
          "tree_id": "ce328203169e4ae251d07def70bfd7839815b428",
